\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Reference measure for real fields}
\date{2026-10-30}

\p{Four real field values on the [four-cycle](fdip-0003) range over an
infinite configuration space. Before weighting configurations by an
action, a reference volume must specify how they are counted. The
[counting-coordinate measure](fdip-002H) assigns volume one to the box
in which each field value lies between zero and one, independently of
the edge weights and mass. It gives infinite volume to the whole space.}

\p{The [real field topology](fdip-002C) and its [Borel sets](fdip-002D)
make coordinate maps measurable. [Reindexing and splitting](fdip-002J)
preserve product volume, while [linear changes](fdip-002K) require a
Jacobian. A [subspace's induced volume](fdip-002M) supplies its own
reference measure. These conventions determine the integrals defining
[positive Gaussian laws](fdip-0017) and [constrained massless laws](fdip-003V).}

